tion/article/top-10-ai-tools-digital-learning-platforms-exam-aspirants-2026/\\\">Candidates preparing for CTET 2026</a> should monitor the official portal at <strong>ctet.nic.in</strong> for schedule updates. All application processes, fee payments, and admit card downloads occur online.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Schedule / Date</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Official Notification &amp; Information Bulletin</td><td>To be announced at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Tentative</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Process Commencement</td><td>To be announced at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Tentative</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Online Application Submission</td><td>To be announced at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Tentati', '8348', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:51:42');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('624', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026 Official Notification: Eligibility, Pattern & Process\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) conducts the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) as a national-level benchmark for assessing the competency of candidates intending to join the teaching profession. Established under the mandate of the Rig', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Eligibility, Exam Pattern & Application Process\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview & Official Announcement</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) conducts the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) as a national-level benchmark to assess teaching candidates. Mandated under the Right to Education (RTE) Act, 2009, CTET serves as a mandatory qualification for teaching positions in Classes I through VIII across Central Government institutions, including Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVS), Navodaya Vidyalayas (NVS), Central Tibetan Schools, and schools in Union Territories (UTs).</p><p>The CTET 2026 notification outlines eligibility, structural frameworks, and evaluation standards. The examination consists of two papers: Paper I for primary stage teachers (Classes I to V) and Paper II for elementary stage teachers (Classes VI to VIII). Candidates fulfilling the required criteria may apply for either paper individually or both simultaneously through the official portal at ctet.nic.in.</p><h2>Important Dates & Timetable</h2><p>Candidates must track the official schedule released by CBSE to ensure timely completion of registration, fee payment, and document uploads. Late submissions will not be entertained under any circumstances.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Schedule</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Official Notification Release</td><td>As per CBSE Portal Schedule</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Commencement</td><td>To be notified at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Form Submission</td><td>As specified on Official Portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Final Date for Fee Payment</td><td>As specified on Official Portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Correction Window</td><td>To be announced post-registration</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Admit Card Generation</td><td>2 Days prior to Examination</td><td>Confirmed</td', '6105', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:52:18');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('625', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Eligibility, Application Process, Exam Pattern & Direct Link\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview &amp; Official AnnouncementThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) conducts the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) under guidelines established by the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE). As mandated under the Right to Education (RTE) Act, passing the CTET is an es', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Check Eligibility & Dates\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 notification will be out soon. Check eligibility criteria for Paper 1 & 2, exam schedule, and apply online at ctet.nic.in.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-ctet-2026-notification-eligibility\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE to announce the CTET 2026 notification soon. Check Paper I & II eligibility, application schedule, and key exam details here.\",\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the official website to apply for CTET 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates can fill out the CTET 2026 application form online on the official portal at ctet.nic.in.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Who is eligible to apply for CTET Paper I (Primary Stage)?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates who have passed Senior Secondary with at least 50% marks and are appearing in or have passed D.El.Ed or B.El.Ed are eligible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is CTET compulsory for teaching in KVS and NVS schools?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, CTET qualification is an essential requirement for teaching recruitment in KVS, NVS, EMRS, and CBSE-affiliated central government schools.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2168', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:52:20');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('626', NULL, NULL, 'topic_analysis', 'Please analyze the following trend:\n\nTREND KEYWORD: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\n\nSOURCE INFORMATION:\nSource Name: National Testing Agency (exams.nta.ac.in)\nSource URL: https://exams.nta.ac.in/NEET/\nSource Snippet: NTA public circular on NEET examination shifts.\n\n\nEXISTING RELATED ARTICLES IN OUR DATABASE:\n- None\n\nReturn your response strictly as a JSON object with this exact schema:\n{\n  \"publish_recommendation\": true/false,\n  \"category\": \"category-slug-from-a', '{\"publish_recommendation\":true,\"category\":\"exam-dates\",\"priority_score\":95,\"reasoning\":\"Statutory public notice from NTA regarding national NEET UG examination shift timings and security guidelines.\",\"suggested_original_angle\":\"Comprehensive candidate instructions and reporting timetable\",\"duplicate_risk\":\"low\",\"source_attribution\":{\"name\":\"National Testing Agency\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/exams.nta.ac.in\\/NEET\\/\",\"reference\":\"NTA\\/NEET-UG\\/2026\\/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01\"}}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:52:58');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('627', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive candidate instructions and reporting timetable\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\",\n    \"source_name\": \"National Testing Agency', '{\"title\":\"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\",\"excerpt\":\"National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially issued comprehensive examination day instructions, shift schedules, and mandatory advisory for NEET UG 2026 aspirants.\",\"content\":\"<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings<\\/h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)<\\/strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas centers are advised to follow official reporting hours strictly.<\\/p><h2>Crucial Examination Day Guidelines<\\/h2><ul><li><strong>Reporting Time:<\\/strong> Candidates must report at examination centers by 11:30 AM for biometric registration.<\\/li><li><strong>Admit Card & ID Proof:<\\/strong> Printed hall ticket along with original Aadhaar card or government photo ID is mandatory.<\\/li><li><strong>Prohibited Items:<\\/strong> Electronic gadgets, smartwatches, and metallic accessories are strictly prohibited inside test halls.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"key_takeaways\":[\"Examination date confirmed for May 03, 2026\",\"Pen and paper mode across all centers\",\"Mandatory biometric verification before entry\"],\"dates_table\":[{\"event\":\"Reporting Time Closes\",\"date\":\"May 03, 2026 (01:30 PM)\",\"status\":\"confirmed\"},{\"event\":\"Examination Timing\",\"date\":\"02:00 PM to 05:20 PM\",\"status\":\"confirmed\"}],\"source_attribution\":{\"name\":\"National Testing Agency\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/exams.nta.ac.in\\/NEET\\/\",\"reference\":\"NTA\\/NEET-UG\\/2026\\/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01\"}}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:52:58');
