ns will not be entertained under any circumstances.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Schedule</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Official Notification Release</td><td>As per CBSE Portal Schedule</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Commencement</td><td>To be notified at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Form Submission</td><td>As specified on Official Portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Final Date for Fee Payment</td><td>As specified on Official Portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Correction Window</td><td>To be announced post-registration</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Admit Card Generation</td><td>2 Days prior to Examination</t', '10336', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:53:01');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('630', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings</h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)</strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across Ind', '{\"edited_title\":\"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\",\"edited_content\":\"<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings<\\/h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)<\\/strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas centers are advised to follow official reporting hours strictly.<\\/p><h2>Crucial Examination Day Guidelines<\\/h2><ul><li><strong>Reporting Time:<\\/strong> Candidates must report at examination centers by 11:30 AM for biometric registration.<\\/li><li><strong>Admit Card & ID Proof:<\\/strong> Printed hall ticket along with original Aadhaar card or government photo ID is mandatory.<\\/li><li><strong>Prohibited Items:<\\/strong> Electronic gadgets, smartwatches, and metallic accessories are strictly prohibited inside test halls.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"readability_score\":95,\"improvements_made\":[\"Structured bullet points for examination day rules\",\"Enhanced lead paragraph readability\"]}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:53:03');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('631', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: December Schedule, Eligibility Criteria & Online Application at ctet.nic.in\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive student instructions\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: December Schedule, Eligibility Criteria & Online Application at', '{\n  \"title\": \"CBSE CTET December 2026: Notification, Eligibility & Apply Online\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE is set to release the CTET December 2026 notification. Check eligibility criteria, exam pattern, and step-by-step online application process here.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) is the premier national-level body responsible for conducting the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET). Established as a mandatory benchmark under the provisions of the Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act, 2009, the CTET serves as a critical qualifying gateway for individuals aspiring to secure teaching positions in central government schools. These include prestigious institutions such as Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVS), Navodaya Vidyalayas (NVS), Central Tibetan Schools, and various schools under the administrative control of Union Territories (UTs) like Delhi, Chandigarh, and Daman &amp; Diu.</p><p>The upcoming CTET December 2026 cycle is designed to assess the pedagogical competence, subject-matter expertise, and psychological aptitude of candidates aiming to teach Classes I through VIII. The examination is divided into two distinct levels: Paper I for primary stage teachers (Classes I to V) and Paper II for elementary stage teachers (Classes VI to VIII). Candidates who meet the eligibility criteria for both levels have the option to appear for both papers. The official notification, comprehensive information bulletin, and online application portal will be hosted exclusively on the official CTET website at <strong>ctet.nic.in</strong>.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education will release the detailed schedule for the CTET December 2026 examination through an official public notice. Aspiring candidates must keep a close watch on the registration timelines, as CBSE does not entertain late submissions u', '6982', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:53:13');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('632', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Eligibility, Exam Pattern & Application Process\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview & Official AnnouncementThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) conducts the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) as a national-level benchmark to assess teaching candidates. Mandated under the Right to Education (RTE) Act, 2009, CTET serves as a mandatory qualification for teaching positio', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Check Eligibility & Apply\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE has released the CTET 2026 notification. Check eligibility criteria, exam pattern, and application process for Paper 1 & 2. Apply online now!\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-ctet-2026-notification\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 notification is out. Learn about the eligibility criteria, exam pattern, important dates, and step-by-step application process here.\",\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Can I apply for both Paper I and Paper II in CTET 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, candidates who meet the eligibility criteria for both primary and elementary stages can apply for Paper I and Paper II simultaneously through the official portal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the official website to apply for CTET 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates can fill out the application form and pay the registration fee online through the official CBSE CTET portal at ctet.nic.in.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is there an upper age limit to apply for the CTET 2026 exam?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, there is no upper age limit prescribed by CBSE for appearing in the CTET exam, provided candidates meet the required educational qualifications.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2203', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:53:28');
