ine Application</td><td>To be updated on ctet.nic.in</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Online Application</td><td>To be updated on ctet.nic.in</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Fee Payment</td><td>To be updated on ctet.nic.in</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Application Correction Window</td><td>To be announced by CBSE</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Release of Admit Card</td><td>2 days before the examination</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>CTET December 2026 Exam Date</td><td>To be scheduled by CBSE</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Declaration of Results</td><td>4 to 6 weeks post-examination</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>CTET Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2><p>Candidates must ', '6661', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:58:18');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('669', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE CTET December 2026: Notification, Eligibility, Exam Pattern & Apply Online\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nCBSE CTET December 2026: OverviewThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) conducts the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) twice a year. This national-level exam determines the eligibility of candidates for teaching positions in classes I to VIII across central government schools like KVS, NVS, ', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE CTET Dec 2026: Notification, Eligibility & Apply\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE CTET December 2026 notification is coming soon. Check eligibility criteria, exam pattern, and learn how to apply online at ctet.nic.in.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-ctet-december-2026-notification\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE will soon release the CTET December 2026 notification. Check eligibility criteria, exam pattern, and application process for Paper I and Paper II.\",\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the difference between CTET Paper I and Paper II?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Paper I is for candidates aspiring to teach Classes I to V (Primary Stage), while Paper II is for those aiming to teach Classes VI to VIII (Elementary Stage).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Can I apply for both CTET Paper I and Paper II?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, candidates who meet the educational eligibility criteria for both levels can opt to apply and appear for both papers.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2537', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:58:39');
