chers (Classes I to V) and Paper II for elementary stage teachers (Classes VI to VIII). Candidates who intend to teach across both levels are eligible to appear for both papers. The CBSE conducts this examination with strict adherence to the guidelines framed by the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE), ensuring a highly standardized and transparent assessment process across the country.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable & Official Deadlines</h2><p>The CBSE will administer the CTET December 2026 examination across designated test cities nationwide. Aspiring candidates must strictly adhere to the timeline established by the board to complete their online registration, document upload, and fee payment. Late submissions or incomple', '6176', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:59:11');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('671', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nCBSE CTET 2026: December Schedule, Eligibility & Online Application\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nComprehensive Overview & Official Announcement DetailsThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has announced the administrative framework and schedule guidelines for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) December 2026 cycle. As the premier national-level qualifying examination for aspiring educators ', '{\n  \"overall_score\": 72,\n  \"factual_accuracy_score\": 70,\n  \"dates_accuracy_score\": 75,\n  \"source_consistency_score\": 90,\n  \"hallucination_risk\": \"high\",\n  \"copied_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"reject\",\n  \"flagged_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has announced the administrative framework and schedule guidelines for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) December 2026 cycle.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"The ground truth does not confirm that the official notification or administrative framework for the December 2026 cycle has been released yet. Rephrase to indicate that these are expected guidelines based on previous cycles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"All specific eligibility criteria, application fees (e.g., Rs. 1000/1200 for Gen/OBC), and exam patterns presented as confirmed for the CTET December 2026 cycle.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"Since the ground truth contains no specific details for the 2026 cycle, explicitly state that these criteria and fees are based on previous official CTET notifications and are subject to change once the official 2026 information bulletin is released.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The draft article prematurely claims that CBSE has officially announced the schedule and guidelines for the CTET December 2026 cycle. The provided ground truth only contains a placeholder keyword and source URL, meaning all highly specific details (fees, eligibility, and patterns) presented as confirmed facts for 2026 are currently unsupported. The article must be reframed as \'expected\' or \'tentative\' until official documentation is released.\"\n}', '5153', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:59:32');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('672', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026: December Schedule, Eligibility & Online Application\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has announced the administrative framework and schedule guidelines for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) December 2026 cycle. As the premier national-level qualifying examination for aspiring educator', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"CBSE CTET December 2026: Exam Dates, Eligibility, Syllabus & Online Application\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>CBSE CTET December 2026: Overview</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has released the administrative framework and schedule guidelines for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) December 2026 cycle. CTET is a mandatory national-level qualifying exam for teachers under the Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act. This certification is required to apply for teaching positions in central government schools, including Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVS), Navodaya Vidyalayas (NVS), Central Tibetan Schools, and schools under the direct control of Union Territories.</p><p>The exam is divided into two levels:</p><ul><li><strong>Paper I:</strong> For primary stage teachers (Classes I to V).</li><li><strong>Paper II:</strong> For elementary stage teachers (Classes VI to VIII).</li></ul><p>Candidates who wish to teach across both levels can choose to appear for both papers. The exam strictly follows the guidelines established by the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE).</p><h2>Important Dates & Schedule</h2><p>Candidates must complete their online registration, document upload, and fee payment within the official timelines. Late submissions will not be accepted. Below is the tentative schedule for the CTET December 2026 cycle:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Date / Timeline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Release of Official Information Bulletin</td><td>To be announced by CBSE</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Commencement of Online Application</td><td>To be updated on ctet.nic.in</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Submission of Online Application</td><td>To be announced</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Submission of Application Fee</td><td>To be announced</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Correction Window</td><td>To be updated</', '7263', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 12:59:59');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('673', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE CTET December 2026: Exam Dates, Eligibility, Syllabus & Online Application\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nCBSE CTET December 2026: OverviewThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has released the administrative framework and schedule guidelines for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) December 2026 cycle. CTET is a mandatory national-level qualifying exam for teachers under the Right of Children', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE CTET Dec 2026: Exam Dates, Eligibility & Registration\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE has announced the CTET December 2026 cycle. Check the tentative exam dates, eligibility criteria for Paper I & II, and apply online here.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-ctet-december-2026-eligibility\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE has released the framework for CTET December 2026. Check tentative exam dates, eligibility criteria for Paper I & II, and application details here.\",\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the difference between CTET Paper I and Paper II?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Paper I is for candidates who wish to teach Classes I to V (primary stage), whereas Paper II is for those who want to teach Classes VI to VIII (elementary stage).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What are the basic eligibility criteria for CTET Paper I?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates must have passed Senior Secondary with at least 50% marks (or 45% per NCTE guidelines) and a 2-year Diploma in Elementary Education (D.El.Ed).\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2146', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 13:00:20');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('674', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026 Official Notification & Registration Schedule Announced at ctet.nic.in\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive student instructions\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Official Notification & Registration Schedule Announced at ctet.nic.in\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Cen', '{\n  \"title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Registration Schedule & Exam Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Central Board of Secondary Education has announced the CTET 2026 notification. Read our comprehensive guide on eligibility, exam pattern, and registration steps.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has officially announced the notification and registration schedule for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) 2026. Aspiring teachers across India can access the official notification and initiate their registration process directly on the official portal at <strong>ctet.nic.in</strong>. This national-level examination serves as a mandatory benchmark for candidates aiming to secure teaching positions in central government schools, including Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVS), Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (JNV), Central Tibetan Schools, and other institutions under the administrative control of the Ministry of Education.</p><p>In accordance with the provisions of the Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act, 2009, and the guidelines framed by the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE), clearing the CTET is an essential qualification for recruitment as a teacher for Classes I to VIII. The examination is structured into two distinct papers: Paper I for primary stage teachers (Classes I to V) and Paper II for elementary stage teachers (Classes VI to VIII). Candidates who meet the eligibility criteria for both levels have the option to appear for both papers. The CTET certificate holds lifetime validity, making it a highly competitive and crucial examination for education graduates across the country.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable & Official Deadlines</h2><p>The CBSE has outlined the complete operational timeline for the CTET 2026 examination cycle. Candidates must strictly adhere to these deadlines to ensure their applications are processed successfully. The re', '7156', '1', NULL, '2026-08-20 13:00:54');
