nt Dates &amp; Official Schedule</h2><p>Candidates must complete all registration, document uploading, fee payment, and hall ticket downloads within the prescribed timelines on the official website.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Date / Window</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Official Notification Release</td><td>Announced on Portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Window</td><td>Refer to ctet.nic.in Schedule</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Fee Payment</td><td>As specified in Schedule</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Correction Window Facility</td><td>To be notified at ctet.nic.in</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Admit Card Release Date</td><td>Prior to', '5126', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:45:34');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('801', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE CTET 2026 Notification Out: Online Registration, Exam Pattern & Eligibility Details\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview &amp; Official AnnouncementThe Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has released the notification and online registration schedule for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) 2026. Interested candidates can review the official information brochure and submit their applications ', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification Out: Apply Online Now\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 notification is out. Check eligibility, exam pattern, and schedule for Paper 1 & 2. Register online at ctet.nic.in today!\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-ctet-2026-online-application\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE releases CTET 2026 notification. Check eligibility criteria, exam pattern, and application steps for Paper 1 and Paper 2 at ctet.nic.in.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"CBSE CTET 2026 notification\",\n    \"CTET 2026 application form\",\n    \"ctet nic in registration 2026\",\n    \"CTET eligibility criteria 2026\",\n    \"CTET paper 1 paper 2 eligibility\",\n    \"how to apply for CTET 2026\",\n    \"CTET exam pattern 2026\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Who is eligible to apply for CTET 2026 Paper 1?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates with Senior Secondary (or equivalent) with at least 50% marks and passed or appearing in the final year of D.El.Ed/B.El.Ed are eligible for Paper 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Can I apply for both Paper 1 and Paper 2 in CTET 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, candidates who meet the educational eligibility for both primary and elementary stages can choose to appear for both papers in a single cycle.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2612', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:46:19');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('802', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026 Notification Released: Registration Schedule, Eligibility & Exam Pattern at ctet.nic.in\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive student instructions\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification Released: Registration Schedule, Eligibility & Exam Pattern at cte', '{\n  \"title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Dates, Eligibility & Pattern at ctet.nic.in\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE has announced the Central Teacher Eligibility Test 2026 schedule. Eligible teaching aspirants can apply online at ctet.nic.in.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has officially released the detailed notification for the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) 2026. Administered in compliance with the statutory guidelines established by the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE), CTET serves as the mandatory benchmark examination for candidates aspiring to secure teaching appointments across primary and upper-primary levels in Indian schools. The official notification and online application portal are accessible via the central web address, <strong>ctet.nic.in</strong>.</p><p>CTET certification is a crucial prerequisite for recruitment as a Primary Teacher (PRT, handling Classes I to V) or an Upper Primary Teacher (TGT, handling Classes VI to VIII) within Central Government recruitment umbrellas including Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (KVS), Navodaya Vidyalaya Samiti (NVS), Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRS), Central Tibetan Schools, and schools functioning under the administrative control of Union Territories (UTs). Furthermore, numerous private institutions and state-level recruitment authorities accept CTET qualification scores for candidate shortlisting.</p><p>As per the policy directive governing national teacher eligibility, the CTET qualifying certificate retains <strong>lifetime validity</strong> across all States and Union Territories. Candidates seeking to improve their existing scores are permitted to re-appear in subsequent editions without any restriction on the maximum number of attempts.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable & Official Deadlines</h2><p>Candidates must carefully review the official registration schedule to ensure all application ', '6467', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:48:13');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('803', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive candidate instructions and reporting timetable\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\",\n    \"source_name\": \"National Testing Agency', '{\n  \"title\": \"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines and Shift Timings Released\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"NTA has issued official examination guidelines and shift timings for NEET UG 2026 under Notice NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01. Read key rules and reporting steps.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has released official instructions and shift schedules for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test for Undergraduate medical admissions (NEET UG 2026) under statutory reference <strong>NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01</strong>. As the designated central testing authority operating under the Ministry of Education and guidance from the National Medical Commission (NMC) and Dental Council of India (DCI), the NTA administers this single nationwide entrance examination to standardize undergraduate medical admissions across India.</p><p>This comprehensive public advisory establishes the operational protocol for millions of medical aspirants seeking admission into MBBS, BDS, BAMS, BHMS, BSMS, BUMS, and BSc Nursing degree programs. The guidelines delineate strict reporting timetables, mandatory identity verification processes, biometrics, security frisking standards, and forbidden items within examination centers across India and international cities. Aspirants competing for seats under the 15% All India Quota (AIQ), 85% State Domicile Quotas, Deemed and Central Universities, ESIC institutes, and Armed Forces Medical College (AFMC) are required to adhere strictly to these published administrative protocols.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>As per Public Notice <strong>NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01</strong>, the NTA conducts the national entrance examination in a single shift in Pen-and-Paper (OMR-based) mode across designated test centers. Candidates must strictly monitor the schedule below to ensure compliance with registration windows, hall ticket download', '5955', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:49:00');
