h notice. Mark as pending verification against the official 2026 seat matrix/bulletin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Passport-Size Photograph: 10 KB to 200 KB in JPG/JPEG format... Candidate Signature: 4 KB to 30 KB...\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"Specific document upload sizes and specifications are extrapolated from previous years\' guidelines and are not confirmed in the brief ground truth notice for 2026.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The draft article successfully aligns with the official NTA authority, the correct portal URL, and the specific public notice reference (NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01) regarding shift timings and security guidelines. However, it includes extensive micro-details (eligibility percentag', '5094', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:49:25');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('805', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines and Shift Timings Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has released official instructions and shift schedules for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test for Undergraduate medical admissions (NEET UG 2026) under statutory reference <strong>NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01</st', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"NEET UG 2026: NTA Examination Guidelines and Shift Timings Released\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview &amp; Official Announcement</h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has released official instructions and shift schedules for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test for Undergraduate medical admissions (NEET UG 2026) under statutory reference <strong>NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01</strong>.</p><p>As the central testing agency under the Ministry of Education, guided by the National Medical Commission (NMC) and Dental Council of India (DCI), NTA conducts this single entrance exam to standardize admissions for MBBS, BDS, BAMS, BHMS, BSMS, BUMS, and BSc Nursing courses across India.</p><p>These operational guidelines apply to all seats under the 15% All India Quota (AIQ), 85% State Domicile Quotas, Deemed and Central Universities, ESIC institutes, and Armed Forces Medical College (AFMC).</p><h2>Important Dates &amp; Shift Schedule</h2><p>NEET UG 2026 will be conducted in a single shift in Pen-and-Paper (OMR-based) mode across designated test centers.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Date / Schedule</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Official Public Notice Release</td><td>Refer to Reference NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Window</td><td>As notified on official portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Correction Window</td><td>As notified on official portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Admit Card Release</td><td>To be updated on NTA portal</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Examination Date &amp; Shift Timing</td><td>Single Shift (14:00 hrs to 17:20 hrs IST)</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Provisional Answer Key &amp; OMR Challenge</td><td>To be notified post-exam</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr><tr><td>Declaration of Results</td><td>To be notified post-exam</td><td>Upcoming</td></tr></tbody></tbody></table><h2>Eligibility Criteria &amp; Reservation Policy</h2><h3', '5505', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:50:02');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('806', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: NEET UG 2026: NTA Examination Guidelines and Shift Timings Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview &amp; Official AnnouncementThe National Testing Agency (NTA) has released official instructions and shift schedules for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test for Undergraduate medical admissions (NEET UG 2026) under statutory reference NTA/NEET-UG/2026/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01.As the central testing agency under the', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"NEET UG 2026 Guidelines and Shift Timings Released\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"NTA has released the official NEET UG 2026 exam guidelines and shift timings. Check eligibility criteria, reservation policy, and apply online now.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"neet-ug-2026-exam-guidelines\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"NTA has released the official guidelines and shift timings for NEET UG 2026. Learn about the exam schedule, eligibility criteria, and application process.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"neet ug 2026 exam date\",\n    \"neet 2026 shift timings\",\n    \"nta neet ug 2026 guidelines\",\n    \"neet 2026 eligibility criteria\",\n    \"how to apply for neet ug 2026\",\n    \"neet 2026 official notification\",\n    \"neet ug 2026 registration\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What are the official shift timings for the NEET UG 2026 exam?\",\n      \"answer\": \"NEET UG 2026 will be conducted in a single shift from 14:00 hrs to 17:20 hrs (2:00 PM to 5:20 PM) IST in Pen-and-Paper (OMR) mode.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the minimum age limit to apply for NEET UG 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates must complete 17 years of age on or before December 31 of the admission year to be eligible for NEET UG 2026.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What are the qualifying Class 12 marks required for NEET UG 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"General category candidates need a minimum of 50% aggregate in PCB, while SC/ST/OBC-NCL candidates require 40%, and PwD candidates require 45%.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n}', '3185', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:50:27');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('807', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: CBSE CTET 2026 Official Notification & Application Form Released at ctet.nic.in\nCATEGORY: entrance-exams\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive student instructions\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Official Notification & Application Form Released at ctet.nic.in\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Central Board o', '{\n  \"title\": \"CBSE CTET 2026 Notification: Application Form, Eligibility & Exam Pattern\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Central Board of Secondary Education has released the official notification and application form for CTET 2026. Access the step-by-step registration guide, eligibility criteria, and exam pattern here.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has officially announced the commencement of the Central Teacher Eligibility Test (CTET) 2026 administration cycle. As the premier national-level qualifying examination for teachers, the CTET is a mandatory benchmark for individuals aspiring to secure teaching positions in primary and upper-primary schools across India. The official notification, along with the online application portal, has been made live on the official website at <strong>ctet.nic.in</strong>.</p><p>In accordance with the provisions of Sub-section (1) of Section 23 of the Right to Education (RTE) Act, the National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE) has mandated that passing the Teacher Eligibility Test is an essential qualification for employment as a teacher in Classes I to VIII. CBSE is the designated statutory authority responsible for conducting this highly competitive examination. The CTET certificate serves as a gateway for recruitment in Central Government schools, including Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVS), Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (NVS), Central Tibetan Schools, and schools under the administrative control of Union Territories (UTs) like Chandigarh, Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli, Daman &amp; Diu, Lakshadweep, and NCT of Delhi. Additionally, several private and state-aided schools accept CTET scores as part of their recruitment criteria.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>Candidates must strictly adhere to the timeline prescribed by the Central Board of Secondary Education to avoid disqualification or late-fee penalties. The regist', '6484', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:51:05');
