dates must be at least 17 years old on or before December 31, 2026.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the minimum qualifying mark in Class 12 for NEET UG 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"General category candidates must secure at least 50% aggregate marks in Physics, Chemistry, and Biology/Biotechnology, while SC/ST/OBC-NCL candidates require a minimum of 40%.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '3017', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:53:29');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('813', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: Official Notice from Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB)\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Direct breakdown of the official RRB CEN notification covering post-wise vacancies, eligibility criteria, zone-wise application steps, and CBT exam stages.\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"Official Notice fro', '{\n  \"title\": \"Official RRB Exam Notification: Vacancies, Eligibility & CBT Stages\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) has issued crucial guidelines for upcoming Centralised Employment Notices (CEN). Learn about eligibility, CBT stages, and application steps.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) functions as the apex regulatory authority responsible for managing the recruitment of Group \'C\' and other technical and non-technical cadres across the vast network of Indian Railways. Operating under the Ministry of Railways, Government of India, the RRB periodically issues Centralised Employment Notices (CEN) to fill critical vacancies in various departments, including engineering, traffic, administration, and technical operations. These recruitment drives attract millions of government job aspirants from every corner of India, making them some of the most competitive examinations globally.</p><p>According to the official updates available on the nodal portal, <strong>rrbcdg.gov.in</strong>, the recruitment process is designed to ensure absolute transparency, meritocracy, and equal opportunity. The board has implemented a robust multi-stage selection framework that leverages advanced technology, including Aadhaar-based biometric verification and multi-session Computer Based Tests (CBT) with standardized normalization procedures. This comprehensive guide provides an in-depth breakdown of the official RRB CEN framework, detailing the eligibility criteria, step-by-step application process, exam patterns, and crucial guidelines for candidates aiming to secure a career in the Indian Railways.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>Candidates must keep a close track of the official timelines released by the Railway Recruitment Control Board. Missing a deadline can result in the forfeiture of the candidature, as the RRB does not entertain', '6242', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:54:08');
