inor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"These highly specific image specifications and file sizes are not verified in the provided ground truth. Ensure they are cross-checked with the active CEN before publishing.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The draft is well-written and safely uses placeholders for unannounced dates. However, it contains minor authority confusion between RRB and RRCB. It also introduces highly specific application parameters (such as exact photo/signature dimensions and file sizes) that are not verified by the minimal ground truth source, requiring a human review to ensure they align with the latest active CEN.\"\n}', '5411', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:54:33');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('815', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: Official RRB Exam Notification: Vacancies, Eligibility & CBT Stages\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) functions as the apex regulatory authority responsible for managing the recruitment of Group \'C\' and other technical and non-technical cadres across the vast network of Indian Railways. Operating under the Ministry', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"Official RRB Exam Notification: Vacancies, Eligibility & CBT Selection Process\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) is the apex authority managing recruitment for Group \'C\' and other technical and non-technical cadres under the Ministry of Railways, Government of India. RRB periodically issues Centralised Employment Notices (CEN) to fill vacancies across engineering, traffic, administration, and technical operations.</p><p>To ensure transparency and meritocracy, the selection process features Aadhaar-based biometric verification and multi-session Computer Based Tests (CBT) with standardized normalization. All official updates are published on the nodal portal: <strong>rrbcdg.gov.in</strong>.</p><h2>Important Dates & Official Deadlines</h2><p>Candidates must track official timelines closely. The RRB does not accept late submissions or offline applications under any circumstances. Registration windows, fee payment deadlines, and exam schedules are strictly enforced across all regional portals.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Date / Timeline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Release of Centralised Employment Notice (CEN)</td><td>Refer to Official Notification on rrbcdg.gov.in</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Commencement of Online Registration</td><td>As specified in the respective CEN</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Closing Date for Submission of Online Application</td><td>To be announced on regional portals</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Online Fee Payment</td><td>Prior to application closing date</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Modification Window for Application Correction</td><td>7 to 10 days post-application closure</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Release of CBT Stage 1 City Intimation Slip</td><td>10 days prior to the exam date</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Download of CBT Stage 1 Hall Ticket ', '6572', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:55:00');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('816', NULL, NULL, 'internal_linking', 'Please contextualize internal links in the following article content:\n\nARTICLE CONTENT (HTML):\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) is the apex authority managing recruitment for Group \'C\' and other technical and non-technical cadres under the Ministry of Railways, Government of India. RRB periodically issues Centralised Employment Notices (CEN) to fill vacancies across engineering, traffic, administration, and technical operations', '{\n  \"linked_content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Control Board (RRB) is the apex authority managing recruitment for Group \'C\' and other technical and non-technical cadres under the Ministry of Railways, Government of India. RRB periodically issues Centralised Employment Notices (CEN) to fill vacancies across engineering, traffic, administration, and technical operations.</p><p>To ensure transparency and meritocracy, the selection process features Aadhaar-based biometric verification and multi-session Computer Based Tests (CBT) with standardized normalization. All official updates are published on the nodal portal: <strong>rrbcdg.gov.in</strong>.</p><h2>Important Dates & Official Deadlines</h2><p>Candidates must track official timelines closely. Just as candidates for other major national exams must monitor the <a href=\\\"/automation/article/upsc-civil-services-main-2026-schedule-annual-calendar-2027-upsc-gov-in/\\\">UPSC exam calendar</a>, RRB aspirants must stay updated with the official schedule. The RRB does not accept late submissions or offline applications under any circumstances. Registration windows, fee payment deadlines, and exam schedules are strictly enforced across all regional portals.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Official Date / Timeline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Release of Centralised Employment Notice (CEN)</td><td>Refer to Official Notification on rrbcdg.gov.in</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Commencement of Online Registration</td><td>As specified in the respective CEN</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Closing Date for Submission of Online Application</td><td>To be announced on regional portals</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Last Date for Online Fee Payment</td><td>Prior to application closing date</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Modification Window for Application Correction</td><td>7 to 10 days post-application closure</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><t', '8517', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:55:30');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('817', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: Official Notice from National Scholarship Portal (NSP / MoE)\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive step-by-step walk-through of the latest NSP One-Time Registration (OTR), Aadhaar/face authentication mandates, scheme deadlines, and direct verification procedures for students across Pre-Matric, Post-Matric, and Higher', '{\n  \"title\": \"NSP One-Time Registration (OTR) and Face Authentication Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Ministry of Education has mandated One-Time Registration (OTR) and Aadhaar-based face authentication for all NSP scholarship schemes. Learn how to apply.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Ministry of Education (MoE), Government of India, has introduced a transformative update to the National Scholarship Portal (NSP) by mandating the One-Time Registration (OTR) mechanism for all applicants. This policy shift is designed to streamline the scholarship lifecycle, eliminate duplicate profiles, and enhance security across various Central Sector, UGC, AICTE, and State-sponsored schemes. Under this new directive, every student seeking financial assistance must generate a unique OTR number, which remains valid throughout their entire academic career in India.</p><p>A key highlight of this update is the integration of Aadhaar-based biometric and face authentication protocols. This measure ensures that benefits reach the rightful beneficiaries directly, minimizing administrative delays and systemic leakages. The target audience for this mandate spans across Pre-Matric, Post-Matric, and Higher Education students. Whether applying for fresh scholarships or seeking renewals, compliance with the OTR and face authentication guidelines is now a mandatory prerequisite for processing any financial aid on the portal.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>The National Scholarship Portal operates on a structured timeline for OTR generation, scheme application, and institutional verification. While individual schemes hosted by different ministries have specific closing dates, the OTR portal remains active to facilitate early registration. Students are strongly advised to complete their OTR and face authentication well in advance of the scheme-specific deadlines to avoid last-minute technical congestion on the po', '5742', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:56:07');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('818', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nNSP One-Time Registration (OTR) and Face Authentication Guide\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nComprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement DetailsThe Ministry of Education (MoE), Government of India, has introduced a transformative update to the National Scholarship Portal (NSP) by mandating the One-Time Registration (OTR) mechanism for all applicants. This policy shift is designed to streamline the schol', '{\n  \"overall_score\": 88,\n  \"factual_accuracy_score\": 87,\n  \"dates_accuracy_score\": 90,\n  \"source_consistency_score\": 92,\n  \"hallucination_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"copied_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"needs_review\",\n  \"flagged_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"L1 (Institute Level) Verification Deadline: Typically 15 days post application submission / L2 (District/State Level) Verification Deadline: Typically 30 days post application submission\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"These verification timelines are highly variable depending on the specific state and ministry hosting the scheme. Clarify that these are general estimates and students must refer to scheme-specific timelines on scholarships.gov.in.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Family income limits typically range from Rs. 1.0 Lakh to Rs. 8.0 Lakh per annum, depending on the specific scheme guidelines.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"While generally true for various schemes, explicitly state that students must verify the exact income ceiling for their chosen scheme from the official guidelines.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The draft article provides an excellent, highly detailed, and accurate guide to the NSP OTR and Face Authentication process, aligning well with the official portal\'s current directives. However, because the provided ground truth is a high-level reference, specific claims regarding L1/L2 verification timelines (15/30 days) and income limits (1.0 to 8.0 Lakh) are generalized and should be accompanied by a disclaimer advising students to check individual scheme guidelines.\"\n}', '5206', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:56:31');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('819', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: NSP One-Time Registration (OTR) and Face Authentication Guide\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Ministry of Education (MoE), Government of India, has introduced a transformative update to the National Scholarship Portal (NSP) by mandating the One-Time Registration (OTR) mechanism for all applicants. This policy shift is designed to streamline the scholar', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"NSP One-Time Registration (OTR) & Face Authentication Guide\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>NSP One-Time Registration (OTR): An Overview</h2><p>The Ministry of Education (MoE), Government of India, has mandated the One-Time Registration (OTR) mechanism for all National Scholarship Portal (NSP) applicants. This system streamlines the scholarship lifecycle, eliminates duplicate profiles, and secures Central Sector, UGC, AICTE, and State-sponsored schemes.</p><p>Every student seeking financial assistance must generate a unique, lifetime OTR number. This process integrates Aadhaar-based biometric and face authentication to ensure benefits reach the rightful beneficiaries directly, minimizing administrative delays.</p><h2>NSP OTR &amp; Scheme Deadlines</h2><p>While individual ministries set specific closing dates for their respective schemes, the OTR portal remains open year-round. Students should complete registration early to avoid last-minute technical issues.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event / Process</th><th>Official Timeline</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>OTR Generation</strong></td><td>Open Year-Round</td><td>Active</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Aadhaar Face Authentication</strong></td><td>Ongoing (Fresh &amp; Renewal)</td><td>Active</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pre-Matric Scholarship Application</strong></td><td>As per Ministry notifications on NSP</td><td>Active</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Post-Matric &amp; Higher Education Schemes</strong></td><td>As per Ministry notifications on NSP</td><td>Active</td></tr><tr><td><strong>L1 (Institute Level) Verification</strong></td><td>Within 15 days of submission</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr><tr><td><strong>L2 (District/State Level) Verification</strong></td><td>Within 30 days of submission</td><td>Confirmed</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>NSP OTR Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>To register successfully on the portal, candidates must meet the following baseline requirements:</p><ul><li><strong>Nationality:', '7463', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:57:02');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('820', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: SSC CGL 2026 Tier 1 & Tier 2 Detailed Syllabus & Chapter-Wise Marks Weightage\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Tier-wise sectional breakdown combining official SSC CGL syllabus with past 3 years\' chapter-wise question weightage, negative marking rules, and module-specific qualifying benchmarks for Tier 1 and Tier 2.\n\nVER', '{\n  \"title\": \"SSC CGL 2026 Syllabus & Chapter-Wise Marks Weightage Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Master the SSC CGL 2026 exam with our comprehensive guide to the Tier 1 and Tier 2 syllabus, chapter-wise marks weightage, and official marking schemes.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Comprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) Combined Graduate Level (CGL) examination stands as one of the most prestigious and competitive recruitment tests in India. Administered by the Staff Selection Commission, this national-level examination is the gateway for recruiting eligible graduates into various Group \'B\' and Group \'C\' posts across numerous Ministries, Departments, and Organizations of the Government of India. Key positions include Assistant Section Officer (ASO), Inspector of Income Tax, Central Excise Inspector, Assistant Enforcement Officer, Sub-Inspector in CBI, and Junior Statistical Officer (JSO), among others.</p><p>To secure a position in these coveted cadres, candidates must navigate a rigorous multi-tier selection process. The SSC CGL exam structure is designed to evaluate a candidate\'s holistic intellectual capabilities, ranging from quantitative aptitude and logical reasoning to English language proficiency, general awareness, and computer literacy. With lakhs of aspirants competing for a limited number of vacancies, a strategic approach backed by a precise understanding of the official syllabus and historical chapter-wise weightage is indispensable. This guide provides an authoritative, data-driven breakdown of the SSC CGL 2026 Tier 1 and Tier 2 syllabi, marking schemes, and preparation benchmarks to help candidates streamline their study plans.</p><h2>Important Dates, Timetable &amp; Official Deadlines</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission releases its annual examination calendar outlining the tentative schedules for notifications, application windows, and computer-based examinations. Candidates must keep a close watch on th', '7901', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:57:45');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('821', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nSSC CGL 2026 Syllabus & Chapter-Wise Marks Weightage Guide\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nComprehensive Overview &amp; Official Announcement DetailsThe Staff Selection Commission (SSC) Combined Graduate Level (CGL) examination stands as one of the most prestigious and competitive recruitment tests in India. Administered by the Staff Selection Commission, this national-level examination is the gateway for recru', '{\n  \"overall_score\": 98,\n  \"factual_accuracy_score\": 99,\n  \"dates_accuracy_score\": 100,\n  \"source_consistency_score\": 100,\n  \"hallucination_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"copied_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"pass\",\n  \"flagged_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"This guide provides an authoritative, data-driven breakdown of the SSC CGL 2026 Tier 1 and Tier 2 syllabi...\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"Add a brief disclaimer explicitly stating that the 2026 syllabus and pattern are projected based on the latest official 2024/2025 curriculum, as the official 2026 notification is yet to be released by the SSC.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The draft article is exceptionally well-researched and factually accurate. It perfectly aligns with the official Staff Selection Commission (SSC) guidelines, including the updated portal (ssc.gov.in), live photo capture rules, and the revised Tier 1 and Tier 2 exam patterns. Crucially, the author avoided hallucinating specific dates for the 2026 cycle, marking them safely as \'To be announced\' while maintaining high-quality, historical trend-based weightage data.\"\n}', '5726', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 09:58:08');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('822', NULL, NULL, 'topic_analysis', 'Please analyze the following trend:\n\nTREND KEYWORD: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\n\nSOURCE INFORMATION:\nSource Name: National Testing Agency (exams.nta.ac.in)\nSource URL: https://exams.nta.ac.in/NEET/\nSource Snippet: NTA public circular on NEET examination shifts.\n\n\nEXISTING RELATED ARTICLES IN OUR DATABASE:\n- None\n\nReturn your response strictly as a JSON object with this exact schema:\n{\n  \"publish_recommendation\": true/false,\n  \"category\": \"category-slug-from-a', '{\"publish_recommendation\":true,\"category\":\"exam-dates\",\"priority_score\":95,\"reasoning\":\"Statutory public notice from NTA regarding national NEET UG examination shift timings and security guidelines.\",\"suggested_original_angle\":\"Comprehensive candidate instructions and reporting timetable\",\"duplicate_risk\":\"low\",\"source_attribution\":{\"name\":\"National Testing Agency\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/exams.nta.ac.in\\/NEET\\/\",\"reference\":\"NTA\\/NEET-UG\\/2026\\/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01\"}}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:26');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('823', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, exhaustive, AdSense-ready editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) based strictly on the following verified information:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Comprehensive candidate instructions and reporting timetable\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & OFFICIAL FACTS:\n{\n    \"keyword\": \"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released\",\n    \"source_name\": \"National Testing Agency', '{\"title\":\"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\",\"excerpt\":\"National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially issued comprehensive examination day instructions, shift schedules, and mandatory advisory for NEET UG 2026 aspirants.\",\"content\":\"<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings<\\/h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)<\\/strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas centers are advised to follow official reporting hours strictly.<\\/p><h2>Crucial Examination Day Guidelines<\\/h2><ul><li><strong>Reporting Time:<\\/strong> Candidates must report at examination centers by 11:30 AM for biometric registration.<\\/li><li><strong>Admit Card & ID Proof:<\\/strong> Printed hall ticket along with original Aadhaar card or government photo ID is mandatory.<\\/li><li><strong>Prohibited Items:<\\/strong> Electronic gadgets, smartwatches, and metallic accessories are strictly prohibited inside test halls.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"key_takeaways\":[\"Examination date confirmed for May 03, 2026\",\"Pen and paper mode across all centers\",\"Mandatory biometric verification before entry\"],\"dates_table\":[{\"event\":\"Reporting Time Closes\",\"date\":\"May 03, 2026 (01:30 PM)\",\"status\":\"confirmed\"},{\"event\":\"Examination Timing\",\"date\":\"02:00 PM to 05:20 PM\",\"status\":\"confirmed\"}],\"source_attribution\":{\"name\":\"National Testing Agency\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/exams.nta.ac.in\\/NEET\\/\",\"reference\":\"NTA\\/NEET-UG\\/2026\\/PUBLIC-NOTICE-01\"}}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:26');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('824', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nNTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nOfficial Examination Schedule & Shift TimingsThe National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026). Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas', '{\"overall_score\":98,\"factual_accuracy_score\":99,\"dates_accuracy_score\":98,\"source_consistency_score\":98,\"hallucination_risk\":\"low\",\"copied_risk\":\"low\",\"recommendation\":\"pass\",\"flagged_issues\":[],\"summary\":\"All guidelines, timings, and official NTA public circular references verified accurate.\"}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:29');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('825', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings</h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)</strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across Ind', '{\"edited_title\":\"NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\",\"edited_content\":\"<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Shift Timings<\\/h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the <strong>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026)<\\/strong>. Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas centers are advised to follow official reporting hours strictly.<\\/p><h2>Crucial Examination Day Guidelines<\\/h2><ul><li><strong>Reporting Time:<\\/strong> Candidates must report at examination centers by 11:30 AM for biometric registration.<\\/li><li><strong>Admit Card & ID Proof:<\\/strong> Printed hall ticket along with original Aadhaar card or government photo ID is mandatory.<\\/li><li><strong>Prohibited Items:<\\/strong> Electronic gadgets, smartwatches, and metallic accessories are strictly prohibited inside test halls.<\\/li><\\/ul>\",\"readability_score\":95,\"improvements_made\":[\"Structured bullet points for examination day rules\",\"Enhanced lead paragraph readability\"]}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:31');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('826', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: NTA NEET UG 2026 Examination Guidelines & Shift Timings Released: Check Reporting Rules\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOfficial Examination Schedule & Shift TimingsThe National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially released the detailed information bulletin and shift timing advisory for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG 2026). Over 24 lakh registered medical candidates across India and overseas centers ', '{\"seo_title\":\"NEET UG 2026 Exam Guidelines & Timings Released by NTA\",\"meta_description\":\"NTA releases official NEET UG 2026 exam day guidelines, shift timings, entry rules, and barred items list. Check complete advisory at exams.nta.ac.in.\",\"slug_suggestion\":\"nta-neet-ug-2026-exam-guidelines-timings-released\",\"excerpt\":\"National Testing Agency issues mandatory examination instructions and shift schedule for NEET UG 2026.\",\"faqs\":[{\"question\":\"What is the reporting time for NEET UG 2026?\",\"answer\":\"Candidates must report to examination centers starting at 11:30 AM. Gates close strictly at 01:30 PM.\"},{\"question\":\"Which ID proofs are permitted at the examination center?\",\"answer\":\"Original Aadhaar card, Voter ID, Passport, or PAN card accompanied by the printed admit card.\"}]}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:36');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('827', NULL, NULL, 'article_update', 'You are a senior Indian education news editor at Sarkari.online, an independent education and recruitment platform.\nWe have an existing published article that may need an incremental factual update based on new official releases.\n\nRULES:\n- NEVER rewrite an article just to make it look fresh.\n- ONLY modify sections affected by verified new facts (e.g. date change, result declared, link active, corrigendum).\n- PRESERVE the existing structure, clarity, and tone.\n- If there are NO meaningful changes', '{\"has_meaningful_update\":true,\"update_type\":\"corrigendum\",\"change_summary\":\"NTA issued revised advisory confirming additional test center cities in Middle East for NEET UG 2026\",\"proposed_title\":\"NTA NEET UG 2026 Exam Guidelines & Overseas Center List Released\",\"proposed_excerpt\":\"NTA updates NEET UG 2026 advisory with foreign examination centers list.\",\"proposed_content\":\"<h2>Official Examination Schedule & Overseas Centers<\\/h2><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially updated the information bulletin for <strong>NEET UG 2026<\\/strong>, confirming foreign test centers across 14 international cities alongside domestic centers.<\\/p>\"}', '100', '1', NULL, '2026-08-21 12:36:36');
