rofessional standards. However, it presents specific scholarship amounts and exam patterns as definitive facts for 2026, which are currently unconfirmed by the 2026 notification. The audit recommends adding disclaimers regarding the provisional nature of these details.\"\n}', '2072', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 04:54:44');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1152', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: PM Yasasvi Scholarship 2026: Class 9 & 11 Eligibility & Grant Details\nCATEGORY: scholarships\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Comprehensive Overview & Official Announcement Details</h2><p>The PM Young Achievers Scholarship Award Scheme for Vibrant India (YASASVI) is a flagship initiative launched by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India. Designed to provide financial impetus to meritorious students from Other Bac', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"PM Yasasvi Scholarship 2026: Eligibility, Application Process & Grant Details\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview of PM YASASVI Scholarship</h2><p>The PM Young Achievers Scholarship Award Scheme for Vibrant India (YASASVI) is an initiative by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment. It provides financial support to students from Other Backward Classes (OBC), Economically Backward Classes (EBC), and Denotified, Nomadic, and Semi-Nomadic Tribes (DNT).</p><p>The National Testing Agency (NTA) conducts the YASASVI Entrance Test (YET) to select beneficiaries. This scheme aims to reduce dropout rates and support students in Class 9 and Class 11 through direct financial assistance.</p><h2>2026 Examination Timeline</h2><p>The official schedule for 2026 will be released by the NTA. Below is the standard operational timeline for the application process:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Notification Release</td><td>To be announced</td></tr><tr><td>Online Application Window</td><td>To be announced</td></tr><tr><td>Correction Window</td><td>To be announced</td></tr><tr><td>Admit Card Release</td><td>15 days prior to exam</td></tr><tr><td>YASASVI Entrance Test (YET)</td><td>To be announced</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>To qualify for the scholarship, applicants must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li><strong>Education:</strong> Currently enrolled in Class 9 or Class 11 at a recognized school.</li><li><strong>Category:</strong> Must belong to OBC, EBC, or DNT categories.</li><li><strong>Income Limit:</strong> Total annual parental/guardian income must not exceed INR 2.5 Lakhs.</li><li><strong>Age:</strong> Must adhere to the age limits specified in the official 2026 information bulletin.</li></ul><h2>How to Apply</h2><ol><li>Visit the official portal: <a href=\\\"https://yet.nta.ac.in\\\">yet.nta.ac.in</a>.</li><li>Click \'New Registration\' to generate login credentials.</li><l', '2382', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 04:54:51');
