photograph, educational certificates, and Aadhaar-linked bank details.</li><li><strong>Select Scheme:</strong> Log in to view schemes matching your profile.</li><li><strong>Submit Application:</strong> Fill in academic and financial details, then submit.</li><li><strong>Save Acknowledgement:</strong> Download the application form for your records and institute submission.</li></ol><h2>Eligibility and Income Limits</h2><p>Eligibility varies by scheme, but applicants must generally meet the following income criteria:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Eligibility</th><th>Income Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pre-Matric</td><td>Class 9-10</td><td>Below 2.5 Lakh/annum</td></tr><tr><td>Post-Matric</td><td>Class 11', '2167', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:43:05');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1243', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: NSP Scholarship 2026-27: Fresh Registration & OTR Guide\nCATEGORY: scholarships\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview of NSP Scholarship 2026-27The National Scholarship Portal (NSP), managed by the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology, has opened registration for the 2026-27 academic session. This unified platform facilitates the disbursement of scholarships from Central and State Governments. As of August 22, 2026, students', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"NSP Scholarship 2026-27: Fresh Registration & OTR Guide\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"Apply for NSP Scholarship 2026-27 online. Follow our step-by-step guide for mandatory OTR registration, eligibility criteria, and document requirements.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"nsp-scholarship-2026-27-registration-guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Learn how to register for the NSP Scholarship 2026-27. Follow our guide for mandatory OTR, eligibility criteria, and the step-by-step application process.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"NSP scholarship 2026-27\",\n    \"NSP OTR registration guide\",\n    \"National Scholarship Portal apply online\",\n    \"NSP scholarship eligibility criteria\",\n    \"how to generate NSP OTR number\",\n    \"NSP scholarship documents required\",\n    \"fresh NSP scholarship registration\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is Aadhaar mandatory for NSP scholarship registration?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, Aadhaar is mandatory for the One-Time Registration (OTR) process and for receiving funds via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Can I apply for multiple scholarship schemes on the NSP portal?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, you can only apply for one scholarship scheme at a time. Submitting multiple applications may lead to the rejection of all your applications.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1345', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:43:12');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1244', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: RRB NTPC 2026 Notification — 10000+ Vacancies Expected, Railway Non-Technical Posts\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: RRB NTPC 2026: expected notification date, vacancy details, eligibility, age limit, exam pattern for Graduate and Undergraduate level posts\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & TOPIC CONTEXT:\n{\n    \"keyword', '{\n  \"title\": \"RRB NTPC 2026 Notification: Expected Vacancies and Exam Details\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Railway Recruitment Board is expected to release the NTPC 2026 notification for 10,000+ vacancies. Learn about eligibility, exam patterns, and preparation.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Overview of RRB NTPC 2026 Recruitment</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) is the primary body responsible for conducting the Non-Technical Popular Categories (NTPC) examination. As of August 22, 2026, candidates across India are awaiting the official notification for the 2026 recruitment cycle. With an anticipated intake of over 10,000 vacancies, this recruitment drive covers various graduate and undergraduate level posts within the Indian Railways. The process is highly competitive, requiring a structured approach to both the Computer Based Test (CBT) 1 and CBT 2 stages.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria and Age Requirements</h2><p>The RRB NTPC recruitment is bifurcated into two distinct categories based on educational qualifications. Candidates must ensure they meet the following criteria before applying:</p><ul><li><strong>Undergraduate Level Posts:</strong> Candidates must have passed 10+2 or its equivalent examination from a recognized board. Age limit is typically 18 to 30 years.</li><li><strong>Graduate Level Posts:</strong> Candidates must hold a Bachelor\'s degree from a recognized university. Age limit is typically 18 to 33 years.</li></ul><p><em>Note: Age relaxation is applicable for reserved categories (SC/ST/OBC-NCL/PwBD) as per the Government of India norms.</em></p><h2>Exam Pattern: CBT 1 and CBT 2</h2><p>The selection process for RRB NTPC involves a two-stage Computer Based Test followed by Document Verification and Medical Examination. The following table outlines the structure based on historical exam patterns.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>CBT 1 (Total Marks)</th><th>CBT 2 (Total Marks)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General Awareness</td><td>40</td><td>50</td></tr><', '2544', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:43:36');
