ture date as a current state of affairs; ensure the tone reflects that the schedule is tentative until the official notification is released.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The article is well-structured and aligns with general UPSC exam patterns. However, it presents a specific day-by-day schedule as a confirmed fact, which is a hallucination risk as the official UPSC timetable for 2026 has not been released. The duration of the exam is also slightly misrepresented as a \'five-day\' event rather than a multi-day process.\"\n}', '1945', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:44:20');
