></tr><tr><td>Day 4</td><td>Afternoon</td><td>GS IV</td></tr><tr><td>Day 5</td><td>Forenoon</td><td>Optional I</td></tr><tr><td>Day 5</td><td>Afternoon</td><td>Optional II</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>General Studies: Thematic Focus Areas</h2><p>While the UPSC does not prescribe a fixed quota of questions, historical trends highlight consistent focus areas for each paper:</p><ul><li><strong>GS Paper I:</strong> Modern History, Geography, and Indian Society.</li><li><strong>GS Paper II:</strong> Constitutional Amendments, Governance, and International Relations.</li><li><strong>GS Paper III:</strong> Budget, Economic Policy, Environment, and Security.</li><li><strong>GS Paper IV:</strong> Ethics and Integrity, with a 50% weigh', '2238', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:44:27');
