 Admit Card</h2><ol><li>Visit the official website: <strong>cbse.gov.in</strong>.</li><li>Navigate to the \'Examination\' or \'Latest @ CBSE\' section.</li><li>Select the link titled \'Date Sheet for Class X and XII Board Examination 2027\'.</li><li>Download the PDF for your records.</li><li><strong>Admit Cards:</strong> Schools will download these via their LOC credentials. Students must collect their printed, signed admit cards directly from their school authorities.</li></ol><h2>Preparation Strategy</h2><p>Complete your NCERT syllabus by November 2026 to allow for revision. Use the following focus areas based on historical trends:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Focus Area</th><th>Strategy</th></tr></thead><tbody', '2226', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:45:11');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1259', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: CBSE Board Exam 2027: Class 10 & 12 Date Sheet Released\nCATEGORY: exam-dates\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview of CBSE Board Examination 2027The Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) has released the official examination schedule for the 2027 academic session. Theory examinations for both Class 10 and Class 12 will commence on February 15, 2027.Examination Schedule and TimingsExams will be conducted in a single shift. Students ', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"CBSE Board Exam 2027 Date Sheet: Class 10 & 12 Schedule\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"CBSE has released the 2027 board exam dates for Class 10 and 12. Check the official schedule, exam timings, and download the date sheet PDF here today.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"cbse-board-exam-2027-date-sheet\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"CBSE has officially released the Class 10 and 12 board exam schedule for 2027. Exams begin February 15; check the full date sheet and exam guidelines here.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"CBSE board exam 2027 date sheet\",\n    \"CBSE class 10 exam date 2027\",\n    \"CBSE class 12 exam date 2027\",\n    \"download CBSE date sheet 2027\",\n    \"CBSE board exam 2027 schedule\",\n    \"CBSE exam pattern 2027\",\n    \"how to download CBSE admit card\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"When will the CBSE 2027 theory examinations commence?\",\n      \"answer\": \"The theory examinations for both Class 10 and Class 12 are scheduled to begin on February 15, 2027.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"How can students obtain their CBSE 2027 admit cards?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Students must collect their printed and signed admit cards directly from their respective school authorities, as schools download them via LOC credentials.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the exam duration and reporting time for CBSE 2027 exams?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Exams are held from 10:30 AM to 1:30 PM; students must be seated by 10:00 AM, with 15 minutes of reading time provided at 10:15 AM.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1525', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:45:15');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1260', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: SSC CGL 2026 Notification Released — 14582 Vacancies, Apply Online at ssc.gov.in by September 30\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Complete SSC CGL 2026 guide: vacancy breakdown, eligibility, age limit, pay scale, exam pattern, and application process for 14,582 Group B & C posts\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & TOPIC ', '{\n  \"title\": \"SSC CGL 2026 Notification: 14,582 Vacancies, Apply by Sept 30\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"The Staff Selection Commission has released the CGL 2026 notification for 14,582 Group B and C posts. Eligible graduates can apply online at ssc.gov.in.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>SSC CGL 2026 Notification Overview</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) has officially released the notification for the Combined Graduate Level (CGL) Examination 2026. This recruitment drive aims to fill 14,582 vacancies across various Group B and Group C posts in ministries, departments, and organizations of the Government of India. Candidates are advised to visit the official website at ssc.gov.in to complete their registration before the deadline of September 30, 2026.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria and Age Limits</h2><p>To be eligible for the SSC CGL 2026, candidates must possess a Bachelor\'s degree from a recognized university or institution. The age limit varies depending on the specific post, generally ranging from 18 to 32 years as of the crucial date specified in the notification. Age relaxation is provided as per government norms: 3 years for OBC candidates and 5 years for SC/ST candidates.</p><h2>Pay Scale and Post Classification</h2><p>The vacancies are categorized under various pay levels ranging from Level 4 to Level 8 of the 7th Central Pay Commission. This includes prestigious positions such as Assistant Audit Officer, Inspector of Income Tax, and various Divisional Accountant roles. The pay scale structure ensures competitive remuneration commensurate with the responsibilities of the respective Group B and C designations.</p><h2>Exam Pattern: Tier-I and Tier-II</h2><p>The selection process is conducted in two primary stages: Tier-I and Tier-II. Tier-I is a Computer-Based Examination (CBE) consisting of objective-type multiple-choice questions. It serves as a qualifying stage for the Tier-II examination. Tier-II is also a Computer-Based Examination, which includes a mandatory Computer ', '2477', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 05:47:31');
