nal Qualification:</strong> Must have passed the Matriculation (Class 10) examination or equivalent from a recognized Board.</li><li><strong>Age Limit:</strong> Generally 18–25 years or 18–27 years, depending on the specific post.</li><li><strong>Age Relaxation:</strong> SC/ST (5 years), OBC (3 years), and PwBD categories receive relaxations as per government norms.</li></ul><h2>Havaldar Physical Standards (PET/PST)</h2><p>The Havaldar post requires qualifying Physical Efficiency and Standard Tests. These are qualifying in nature and do not contribute to the final merit list.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Walking (PET)</th><th>Height (PST)</th><th>Chest (PST)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Male</td><td>160', '2583', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:07:14');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1399', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: SSC MTS & Havaldar 2026: Official Notification, Eligibility, and Selection Guide\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview of SSC MTS and Havaldar Recruitment 2026The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) has launched the 2026 recruitment cycle for Multi-Tasking (Non-Technical) Staff and Havaldar (CBIC & CBN). This is a matriculation-level recruitment opportunity. As of August 22, 2026, candidates are advised to complete', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"SSC MTS & Havaldar 2026: Official Notification & Guide\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"Check SSC MTS & Havaldar 2026 notification, eligibility, and exam pattern. Complete your mandatory OTR on ssc.gov.in to apply for these 10th-pass jobs.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"ssc-mts-havaldar-2026-notification\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Get the latest updates on SSC MTS & Havaldar 2026 recruitment. Learn about eligibility, the mandatory OTR process, physical standards, and exam patterns.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"SSC MTS 2026 notification\",\n    \"SSC Havaldar recruitment 2026\",\n    \"SSC MTS eligibility criteria\",\n    \"how to do SSC OTR registration\",\n    \"SSC MTS exam pattern 2026\",\n    \"SSC MTS application process\",\n    \"Havaldar physical test standards\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is One-Time Registration (OTR) mandatory for SSC MTS 2026?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, OTR is mandatory for all candidates on the new SSC portal (ssc.gov.in) to apply for any recruitment cycle, including SSC MTS and Havaldar.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Do physical tests for Havaldar count towards the final merit list?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, the Physical Efficiency Test (PET) and Physical Standard Test (PST) for the Havaldar post are only qualifying in nature and do not affect the final merit list.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1422', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:07:18');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1400', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: SSC GD Constable 2026: State-Wise Vacancies, Physical Standards & Exam Blueprint\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: Provide a state-wise vacancy breakdown and a simplified physical efficiency test (PET/PST) checklist to help candidates assess their eligibility and regional competition levels.\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DAT', '{\n  \"title\": \"SSC GD Constable 2026: Vacancies, Physical Standards & Exam Blueprint\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"A comprehensive guide to the SSC GD Constable 2026 recruitment, covering state-wise vacancy trends, physical eligibility criteria, and the exam blueprint.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Overview of SSC GD Constable 2026 Recruitment</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) conducts the General Duty (GD) Constable recruitment to fill vacancies in various Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) including the BSF, CISF, CRPF, SSB, ITBP, AR, and SSF. As of August 22, 2026, candidates must align their preparation with the official notification guidelines. This recruitment process is highly competitive, and understanding the regional vacancy distribution and physical standards is critical for success.</p><h2>Understanding State-Wise Vacancy Distribution</h2><p>Vacancies for SSC GD Constable are determined based on the requirements of the participating forces and are distributed across states and Union Territories. While the final vacancy count is subject to change based on the Ministry of Home Affairs\' directives, candidates should monitor the official SSC portal for state-specific updates. The competition level varies significantly by state, often influenced by the density of applicants and the specific regional quotas allocated to Naxal/Militancy affected districts and Border districts.</p><h3>Trend-Based Historical Distribution (Based on Past Exam Papers)</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Estimated Weightage in Selection</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General Intelligence & Reasoning</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>General Knowledge & Awareness</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>Elementary Mathematics</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>English/Hindi Language</td><td>25%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Note: The SSC does not prescribe a fixed per-chapter quota. The table above represents the standard distribution of questions across the four sections of the Computer Based Examination (CBE).</p', '2427', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:07:28');
