INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1407', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: RRB Group D 2026: PET Standards and Selection Rules Guide\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Overview of RRB Group D 2026 Selection Process</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) conducts the Level 1 recruitment process through a multi-stage selection procedure. Following the Computer Based Test (CBT), candidates are shortlisted for the Physical Efficiency Test (PET). As of August 22, 2026, candidates must understa', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"RRB Group D 2026: PET Standards and Selection Guidelines\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview of RRB Group D 2026 Selection Process</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Level 1 recruitment follows a multi-stage process. After the Computer Based Test (CBT), shortlisted candidates must clear the Physical Efficiency Test (PET). As of August 22, 2026, the PET is a mandatory qualifying stage; failure to meet these standards results in immediate disqualification, regardless of CBT performance.</p><h2>Physical Efficiency Test (PET) Standards</h2><p>The PET evaluates the physical endurance required for railway duties. Requirements differ by gender. Candidates should begin training early, as the window between CBT results and PET dates is typically short.</p><h3>PET Requirements for Male Candidates</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Standard</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Weight Carrying</td><td>35 kg for 100 meters in 2 minutes (single attempt)</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>1000 meters in 4 minutes and 15 seconds (single attempt)</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>PET Requirements for Female Candidates</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Standard</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Weight Carrying</td><td>20 kg for 100 meters in 2 minutes (single attempt)</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>1000 meters in 5 minutes and 40 seconds (single attempt)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Selection Rules and Merit Calculation</h2><p>Final selection is based on the merit list generated from the CBT. The PET is strictly qualifying in nature.</p><ul><li><strong>Shortlisting Ratio:</strong> RRBs shortlist candidates for the PET at a 3:1 ratio against total vacancies.</li><li><strong>Qualifying Nature:</strong> PET marks are not added to the final merit list.</li><li><strong>Document Verification (DV):</strong> Only PET qualifiers proceed to Document Verification and the Medical Examination.</li></ul><h2>Preparation Strategy</h2><ol><li><strong>Endurance Building:</str', '1930', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:10');
