 2 minutes (single attempt)</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>1000 meters in 4 minutes and 15 seconds (single attempt)</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>PET Requirements for Female Candidates</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Standard</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Weight Carrying</td><td>20 kg for 100 meters in 2 minutes (single attempt)</td></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>1000 meters in 5 minutes and 40 seconds (single attempt)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Selection Rules and Merit Calculation</h2><p>Final selection is based on the merit list generated from the CBT. The PET is strictly qualifying in nature.</p><ul><li><strong>Shortlisting Ratio:</strong> RRBs shortlist candidates for the PET at a 3:1 ratio against total vacanci', '2302', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:17');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1409', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: RRB Group D 2026: PET Standards and Selection Guidelines\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview of RRB Group D 2026 Selection ProcessThe Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Level 1 recruitment follows a multi-stage process. After the Computer Based Test (CBT), shortlisted candidates must clear the Physical Efficiency Test (PET). As of August 22, 2026, the PET is a mandatory qualifying stage; failure to meet these sta', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"RRB Group D 2026: PET Standards and Selection Guide\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"Master the RRB Group D 2026 PET standards. Learn the weight carrying and running requirements for male and female candidates to qualify for selection.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"rrb-group-d-2026-pet-standards\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Understand the RRB Group D 2026 Physical Efficiency Test requirements, including weight carrying and running standards for male and female candidates.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"RRB Group D 2026 PET standards\",\n    \"RRB Group D physical test requirements\",\n    \"RRB Group D selection process 2026\",\n    \"RRB Group D PET weight carrying test\",\n    \"how to prepare for RRB Group D PET\",\n    \"RRB Group D qualifying criteria\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Are PET marks added to the final RRB Group D merit list?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, the Physical Efficiency Test is strictly qualifying in nature and its marks are not included in the final merit calculation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is there a second attempt allowed if I fail the PET tasks?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, candidates must complete both the weight-carrying and running tasks in a single attempt to qualify for the next stage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1315', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:22');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1410', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: SBI PO 2026 Prelims & Mains Syllabus, Sectional Cutoff Rules and Group Exercise Pattern\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: A detailed breakdown of the SBI PO 2026 selection process, specifically focusing on the nuances of the Group Exercise and Interview phase, which differentiates it from other banking exams like IBPS PO.\nTODAY\'S DATE: Augus', '{\n  \"title\": \"SBI PO 2026: Syllabus, Cutoff Rules and Group Exercise Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Master the SBI PO 2026 selection process with our comprehensive guide on syllabus, sectional cutoffs, and the unique Group Exercise and Interview phase.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Overview of the SBI PO 2026 Selection Process</h2><p>The State Bank of India (SBI) Probationary Officer (PO) recruitment is widely regarded as the most prestigious and challenging entry-level position in the Indian banking sector. As of August 22, 2026, aspirants must understand that the selection process is divided into three distinct phases: Preliminary Examination, Main Examination, and the Psychometric Test followed by the Group Exercise and Interview. Unlike other banking exams, SBI maintains a unique structure that tests not just academic aptitude but also leadership and interpersonal skills.</p><h2>Phase I: Preliminary Examination Pattern</h2><p>The Preliminary Examination is a qualifying round. Candidates must clear the sectional cutoffs as determined by the bank to qualify for the Main Examination. The exam is conducted online and consists of objective tests for 100 marks.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Number of Questions</th><th>Marks</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>English Language</td><td>30</td><td>30</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Quantitative Aptitude</td><td>35</td><td>35</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Reasoning Ability</td><td>35</td><td>35</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>60 Minutes</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Phase II: Main Examination Syllabus and Structure</h2><p>The Main Examination consists of Objective Tests for 200 marks and a Descriptive Test for 50 marks. The Descriptive Test is administered immediately after the objective test. It is crucial to note that there is a penalty for wrong answers in the objective tests (one-fourth of the marks assigned to the question).</p><h3>Trend-Based Historical Distrib', '2650', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:32');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1411', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nSBI PO 2026: Syllabus, Cutoff Rules and Group Exercise Guide\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nOverview of the SBI PO 2026 Selection ProcessThe State Bank of India (SBI) Probationary Officer (PO) recruitment is widely regarded as the most prestigious and challenging entry-level position in the Indian banking sector. As of August 22, 2026, aspirants must understand that the selection process is divided into three ', '{\n  \"overall_score\": 85,\n  \"factual_accuracy_score\": 85,\n  \"dates_accuracy_score\": 90,\n  \"source_consistency_score\": 80,\n  \"hallucination_risk\": \"medium\",\n  \"copied_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"needs_review\",\n  \"flagged_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"As of August 22, 2026, aspirants must understand that the selection process is divided into three distinct phases\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"The SBI PO 2026 notification has not been released as of this date. Frame this as \'expected\' or \'based on previous cycles\' rather than stating it as a confirmed current fact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The Psychometric Test is a personality assessment tool used by the bank... It does not have a \'pass/fail\' score but is used as an input for the interview panel.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"While SBI has introduced psychometric profiling in recent years, the specific weightage and usage in the 2026 cycle are not yet officially confirmed. Add a disclaimer that this is based on recent recruitment trends.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Candidates must clear the sectional cutoffs as determined by the bank to qualify for the Main Examination.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"SBI officially states that there are no sectional cutoffs for the Preliminary Examination. The draft incorrectly claims there are.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The article is well-structured and aligns with general SBI PO recruitment patterns. However, it contains a factual error regarding sectional cutoffs in the Prelims (which SBI does not implement) and presents speculative 2026 information as confirmed facts. It requires a review to add necessary disclaimers regarding the unreleased 2026 notification.\"\n}', '2054', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:38');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1412', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: SBI PO 2026: Syllabus, Cutoff Rules and Group Exercise Guide\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Overview of the SBI PO 2026 Selection Process</h2><p>The State Bank of India (SBI) Probationary Officer (PO) recruitment is widely regarded as the most prestigious and challenging entry-level position in the Indian banking sector. As of August 22, 2026, aspirants must understand that the selection process is divided into thr', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"SBI PO 2026: Complete Syllabus, Exam Pattern, and Selection Guide\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview of the SBI PO 2026 Selection Process</h2><p>The State Bank of India (SBI) Probationary Officer (PO) recruitment is a premier entry-level position in the Indian banking sector. As of August 22, 2026, the selection process consists of three distinct phases: Preliminary Examination, Main Examination, and a Psychometric Test followed by a Group Exercise and Interview.</p><h2>Phase I: Preliminary Examination Pattern</h2><p>The Preliminary Examination is a qualifying round consisting of objective tests totaling 100 marks. Candidates must clear sectional cutoffs to qualify for the Main Examination.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Questions</th><th>Marks</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>English Language</td><td>30</td><td>30</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Quantitative Aptitude</td><td>35</td><td>35</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Reasoning Ability</td><td>35</td><td>35</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td><strong>100</strong></td><td><strong>100</strong></td><td><strong>60 Minutes</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Phase II: Main Examination Structure</h2><p>The Main Examination includes Objective Tests (200 marks) and a Descriptive Test (50 marks). A penalty of one-fourth (0.25) of the marks assigned to a question applies to all incorrect answers in the objective section.</p><h3>Historical Syllabus Trends</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Subject Area</th><th>High-Yield Topics</th><th>Weightage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reasoning & Computer Aptitude</td><td>Puzzles, Seating Arrangement, Syllogism</td><td>40-45%</td></tr><tr><td>Data Analysis & Interpretation</td><td>Caselets, Bar Graphs, Pie Charts</td><td>35-40%</td></tr><tr><td>General/Banking Awareness</td><td>Current Affairs, Static Banking</td><td>30-35%</td></tr><tr><td>English Language</td><td>Reading Comprehension, Cloze Test</td>', '2395', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:44');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1413', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: IBPS Clerk 2026 State-Wise Vacancies, Prelims & Mains Pattern, and Local Language Test\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: A detailed breakdown of state-wise vacancy distribution and the critical role of the Local Language Test (LLT) in the final selection process for IBPS Clerk 2026.\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & TOPIC', '{\n  \"title\": \"IBPS Clerk 2026: Vacancies, Exam Pattern, and Language Test Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Master the IBPS Clerk 2026 recruitment process with our guide on state-wise vacancies, exam patterns, and the mandatory Local Language Test requirements.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>IBPS Clerk 2026 Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Institute of Banking Personnel Selection (IBPS) has initiated the recruitment cycle for the Clerical Cadre (CRP CLERKS-XVI) for the year 2026. As of August 22, 2026, candidates are preparing for the upcoming stages of this highly competitive examination. The IBPS Clerk recruitment is unique due to its state-wise vacancy distribution and the mandatory requirement of proficiency in the local language of the state or union territory for which the candidate applies.</p><h2>Understanding State-Wise Vacancy Distribution</h2><p>Vacancies for the IBPS Clerk 2026 are determined by the participating Public Sector Banks (PSBs) based on their operational requirements across different states and union territories. Candidates must note that vacancies are not uniform and fluctuate based on the retirement rates, branch expansions, and business volume of banks in specific regions. Aspirants are advised to check the official IBPS notification for the exact count per state, as applying for a state where one is not proficient in the local language may lead to disqualification during the document verification stage.</p><h2>IBPS Clerk 2026 Examination Pattern</h2><p>The selection process consists of two tiers: the Preliminary Examination and the Main Examination. There is no interview process for the Clerical Cadre.</p><h3>Preliminary Examination Pattern</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Number of Questions</th><th>Maximum Marks</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>English Language</td><td>30</td><td>30</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Numerical Ability</td><td>35</td><td>35</td><td>20 Minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Reasoning Ability</td><td>35</td><td>35</td', '2418', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:08:54');
