merit and is divided into two parts.</p><h3>Part A: Merit-Based</h3><ul><li>Mathematics: 25 Questions</li><li>General Intelligence & Reasoning: 25 Questions</li><li>Basic Science & Engineering: 40 Questions</li><li>General Awareness & Current Affairs: 10 Questions</li></ul><h3>Part B: Qualifying Trade Test</h3><p>Part B is specific to your ITI/Trade discipline. Candidates must secure a minimum of 35% marks to qualify. Failure to pass Part B results in immediate disqualification, regardless of your score in Part A.</p><h2>Computer Based Aptitude Test (CBAT / Psycho Test)</h2><p>The CBAT evaluates cognitive abilities such as memory, observation, and spatial perception. There is no negative marking in this stage. Candidates m', '2529', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:12:39');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1442', NULL, NULL, 'seo_generation', 'Please generate SEO metadata for this article:\n\nARTICLE TITLE: RRB ALP 2026: Complete Exam Pattern Guide for CBT 1, CBT 2, and Psycho Test\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nARTICLE CONTENT EXCERPT:\nOverview of the RRB ALP 2026 Selection ProcessThe Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Assistant Loco Pilot (ALP) examination is a multi-stage process testing technical aptitude, reasoning, and psychological readiness. As of August 22, 2026, the selection consists of three Computer Based Tests (CBTs), followed by ', '{\n  \"seo_title\": \"RRB ALP 2026 Exam Pattern: CBT 1, CBT 2 & Psycho Guide\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"Master the RRB ALP 2026 exam pattern. Get detailed insights on CBT 1, CBT 2, trade tests, and psycho test requirements to boost your selection chances.\",\n  \"slug_suggestion\": \"rrb-alp-2026-exam-pattern-guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Understand the complete RRB ALP 2026 selection process, including CBT 1 screening, CBT 2 technical core, and the mandatory Computer Based Aptitude Test.\",\n  \"target_keywords\": [\n    \"RRB ALP 2026 exam pattern\",\n    \"RRB ALP selection process\",\n    \"RRB ALP CBT 1 syllabus\",\n    \"RRB ALP CBT 2 exam details\",\n    \"RRB ALP psycho test guide\",\n    \"how to prepare for RRB ALP\",\n    \"RRB ALP trade test qualifying marks\"\n  ],\n  \"faqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Are marks from CBT 1 included in the final RRB ALP merit list?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, CBT 1 is strictly a screening stage used to shortlist candidates for CBT 2; its marks are not counted toward the final merit list.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the minimum qualifying score for the RRB ALP Part B trade test?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Candidates must secure a minimum of 35% marks in the Part B trade test to qualify, regardless of their performance in Part A.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is there negative marking in the RRB ALP Computer Based Aptitude Test?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No, there is no negative marking in the Computer Based Aptitude Test (CBAT), though candidates must achieve a minimum T-score of 42 in each test battery.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1458', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:12:45');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1443', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: RRB Junior Engineer (JE) 2026: Technical Syllabus & Stage-Wise Selection Process\nCATEGORY: government-jobs\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: A detailed breakdown of the 2026 technical syllabus with a focus on high-weightage topics and a simplified stage-wise selection roadmap to help candidates streamline their preparation.\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOU', '{\n  \"title\": \"RRB Junior Engineer 2026: Technical Syllabus & Selection Roadmap\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Master the RRB JE 2026 technical syllabus and selection process with our comprehensive guide. Get expert insights on high-yield topics and exam strategy.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Overview of RRB Junior Engineer 2026 Recruitment</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Junior Engineer (JE) examination remains one of the most sought-after technical recruitment drives in India. As of August 22, 2026, candidates preparing for the upcoming cycles must align their preparation with the standardized technical syllabus prescribed by the RRB. The selection process is rigorous, designed to test both general aptitude and core engineering proficiency across various disciplines including Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, and Electronics Engineering.</p><h2>Stage-Wise Selection Process</h2><p>The RRB JE selection process is conducted in two distinct stages, followed by Document Verification and Medical Examination. Understanding this roadmap is critical for strategic planning.</p><ul><li><strong>First Stage CBT:</strong> This is a screening stage. It consists of 100 questions covering Mathematics, General Intelligence & Reasoning, General Awareness, and General Science. Marks obtained here are not counted toward the final merit list.</li><li><strong>Second Stage CBT:</strong> This is the decisive stage. It includes 150 questions, with a heavy emphasis on the Technical Abilities section (100 questions). Only candidates who qualify in the first stage are eligible to appear for this.</li><li><strong>Document Verification (DV):</strong> Candidates are shortlisted based on their performance in the Second Stage CBT.</li><li><strong>Medical Examination:</strong> Final selection is subject to the candidate meeting the prescribed medical standards for the specific post.</li></ul><h2>Technical Syllabus Breakdown</h2><p>The Technical Abilities section in the Second Stage CBT is discipline-specific. While', '2345', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:12:55');
