e CBT.</li><li><strong>Medical Examination:</strong> Final appointment is subject to meeting the medical standards prescribed for the specific post.</li></ul><h2>Technical Syllabus Breakdown</h2><p>The Technical Abilities section is discipline-specific. While the RRB provides a broad syllabus, candidates should prioritize core engineering fundamentals based on historical trends.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Discipline</th><th>Key Focus Areas</th><th>Weightage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Civil Engineering</td><td>Surveying, Concrete Technology, Soil Mechanics, Hydraulics</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical Engineering</td><td>Thermodynamics, Theory of Machines, Fluid Mechanics, Manufacturing</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>', '1991', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:13:06');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1446', NULL, NULL, 'internal_linking', 'Please contextualize internal links in the following article content:\n\nARTICLE CONTENT (HTML):\n<h2>Overview of RRB Junior Engineer 2026 Recruitment</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Junior Engineer (JE) examination is a premier technical recruitment drive in India. As of August 22, 2026, candidates should align their preparation with the standardized technical syllabus. The selection process evaluates both general aptitude and core engineering proficiency across Civil, Mechanical, Elect', '{\n  \"linked_content\": \"<h2>Overview of RRB Junior Engineer 2026 Recruitment</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Junior Engineer (JE) examination is a premier technical recruitment drive in India. As of August 22, 2026, candidates should align their preparation with the standardized technical syllabus. The selection process evaluates both general aptitude and core engineering proficiency across Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, and Electronics disciplines. For those also exploring other competitive government opportunities, you may want to check the <a href=\\\"/automation/article/ssc-cgl-2026-notification-apply/\\\">SSC CGL 2026 Notification</a> for upcoming vacancies.</p><h2>Stage-Wise Selection Process</h2><p>The selection process consists of two Computer Based Tests (CBTs), followed by Document Verification and a Medical Examination.</p><ul><li><strong>First Stage CBT (Screening):</strong> Comprises 100 questions covering Mathematics, General Intelligence & Reasoning, General Awareness, and General Science. Marks from this stage are not included in the final merit list.</li><li><strong>Second Stage CBT (Decisive):</strong> Comprises 150 questions, with 100 questions dedicated to Technical Abilities. Only candidates who qualify in the first stage are eligible.</li><li><strong>Document Verification (DV):</strong> Shortlisting is based on performance in the Second Stage CBT.</li><li><strong>Medical Examination:</strong> Final appointment is subject to meeting the medical standards prescribed for the specific post.</li></ul><h2>Technical Syllabus Breakdown</h2><p>The Technical Abilities section is discipline-specific. While the RRB provides a broad syllabus, candidates should prioritize core engineering fundamentals based on historical trends. Students interested in broader engineering entrance exams can also review the <a href=\\\"/automation/article/jee-main-2027-syllabus-weightage/\\\">JEE Main 2027 syllabus</a> to understand how technical weightage is structured in c', '2538', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:13:12');
