nical discipline.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '1268', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:13:16');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1448', NULL, NULL, 'article_generation', 'Please generate an in-depth, highly structured, AdSense-compliant editorial article (aim for 1000+ words) tailored to the topic:\n\nTOPIC / HEADLINE: UGC NET 2026: Paper 1 Teaching Aptitude Syllabus, JRF Cutoff Percentiles & Validity\nCATEGORY: exam-results\nEDITORIAL FOCUS: A deep-dive analysis of the 2026 syllabus changes for Paper 1, combined with a data-driven breakdown of JRF cutoff trends to help aspirants set realistic target scores.\nTODAY\'S DATE: August 22, 2026\n\nVERIFIED SOURCE DATA & TOPIC', '{\n  \"title\": \"UGC NET 2026: Paper 1 Syllabus, JRF Cutoffs & Preparation Guide\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"Master the UGC NET 2026 Paper 1 syllabus and analyze historical JRF cutoff trends to optimize your preparation strategy for the upcoming examination cycle.\",\n  \"content\": \"<h2>Overview of UGC NET 2026 Paper 1</h2><p>The University Grants Commission National Eligibility Test (UGC NET) remains the definitive benchmark for determining the eligibility of Indian nationals for Assistant Professor positions and Junior Research Fellowship (JRF) awards in Indian universities and colleges. As of August 22, 2026, candidates must align their preparation with the standardized syllabus prescribed by the National Testing Agency (NTA). Paper 1 is common to all candidates, designed to assess teaching and research aptitude, reasoning ability, and general awareness.</p><h2>Detailed Syllabus Breakdown: Teaching Aptitude</h2><p>Teaching Aptitude constitutes a significant portion of Paper 1. The syllabus is structured to evaluate a candidate\'s pedagogical knowledge and classroom management skills. Key units include:</p><ul><li><strong>Teaching:</strong> Concept, objectives, levels of teaching (memory, understanding, and reflective), and characteristics of learners.</li><li><strong>Learner Characteristics:</strong> Academic, social, emotional, and cognitive characteristics of adolescent and adult learners.</li><li><strong>Factors Affecting Teaching:</strong> Teacher, learner, support material, instructional facilities, learning environment, and institution.</li><li><strong>Methods of Teaching:</strong> Teacher-centered vs. learner-centered methods, offline vs. online methods (SWAYAM, SWAYAMPRABHA, MOOCs).</li><li><strong>Teaching Support System:</strong> Traditional, modern, and ICT-based tools.</li><li><strong>Evaluation Systems:</strong> Elements, types, and trends in evaluation, including Choice Based Credit System (CBCS) and computer-based testing.</li></ul><h2>Trend-Based Historical Distribu', '2584', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:13:27');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1449', NULL, NULL, 'fact_checking', 'Please perform a rigorous factual audit on the following draft article:\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE TITLE:\nUGC NET 2026: Paper 1 Syllabus, JRF Cutoffs & Preparation Guide\n\nDRAFT ARTICLE CONTENT:\nOverview of UGC NET 2026 Paper 1The University Grants Commission National Eligibility Test (UGC NET) remains the definitive benchmark for determining the eligibility of Indian nationals for Assistant Professor positions and Junior Research Fellowship (JRF) awards in Indian universities and colleges. As of August 22, ', '{\n  \"overall_score\": 92,\n  \"factual_accuracy_score\": 95,\n  \"dates_accuracy_score\": 95,\n  \"source_consistency_score\": 90,\n  \"hallucination_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"copied_risk\": \"low\",\n  \"recommendation\": \"pass\",\n  \"flagged_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"As of August 22, 2026, candidates must align their preparation with the standardized syllabus prescribed by the National Testing Agency (NTA).\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"The date \'August 22, 2026\' is specific but lacks a corresponding official NTA notification reference in the ground truth; ensure this date aligns with the actual NTA exam calendar release.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"For 2026, candidates should aim for a percentile score above 98.0 to ensure a competitive edge for JRF.\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"While helpful advice, clarify that this is an aspirational target based on historical trends rather than an official NTA-prescribed benchmark.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The article is well-structured and aligns with standard UGC NET procedures. It correctly identifies the NTA as the authority and accurately reflects the syllabus structure. The minor issues relate to the presentation of aspirational targets as potential facts, which should be framed more clearly as historical estimates.\"\n}', '1913', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:13:32');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1450', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: UGC NET 2026: Paper 1 Syllabus, JRF Cutoffs & Preparation Guide\nCATEGORY: exam-results\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Overview of UGC NET 2026 Paper 1</h2><p>The University Grants Commission National Eligibility Test (UGC NET) remains the definitive benchmark for determining the eligibility of Indian nationals for Assistant Professor positions and Junior Research Fellowship (JRF) awards in Indian universities and colleges. As of August 22, ', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"UGC NET 2026: Paper 1 Syllabus, JRF Cutoffs & Preparation Guide\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview of UGC NET 2026 Paper 1</h2><p>The UGC NET is the benchmark for Assistant Professor eligibility and Junior Research Fellowship (JRF) awards in India. As of August 22, 2026, candidates must follow the NTA-prescribed syllabus. Paper 1 is a common, mandatory paper designed to assess teaching aptitude, research skills, reasoning, and general awareness.</p><h2>Teaching Aptitude: Syllabus Breakdown</h2><p>This section evaluates pedagogical knowledge and classroom management. Key focus areas include:</p><ul><li><strong>Teaching:</strong> Objectives, levels (memory, understanding, reflective), and learner characteristics.</li><li><strong>Factors Affecting Teaching:</strong> Teacher, learner, support materials, and learning environment.</li><li><strong>Methods:</strong> Teacher-centered vs. learner-centered, and digital platforms (SWAYAM, MOOCs).</li><li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Trends in testing, including CBCS and computer-based evaluation.</li></ul><h2>Paper 1 Question Distribution</h2><p>While the NTA does not mandate a fixed quota, historical trends indicate the following distribution for the 50-question paper:</p><table><thea