ritical pathway\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"unsupported_claim\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"correction_advice\": \"Ensure the date reflects the current status of the portal; if the portal is closed, this should be explicitly stated to avoid misleading applicants.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The article is well-structured and aligns with the general framework of the PMSSS. However, it contains specific claims regarding income ceilings and entrance exam requirements that require verification against the official 2026 AICTE notification to avoid potential misinformation. The procedural steps are logically sound but should be cross-referenced with the latest AICTE portal guidelines.\"\n}', '2003', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:14:07');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1455', NULL, NULL, 'content_editing', 'Please polish and editorially enhance this draft article:\n\nHEADLINE: PMSS 2026: Eligibility, Benefits, and Application Guide\nCATEGORY: scholarships\n\nRAW CONTENT:\n<h2>Overview of the Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) 2026</h2><p>The Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) is a flagship initiative administered by the All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) under the Ministry of Education, Government of India. Designed specifically for students from the Union Ter', '{\n  \"edited_title\": \"PMSSS 2026: Eligibility, Benefits, and Application Guide\",\n  \"edited_content\": \"<h2>Overview of the Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) 2026</h2><p>The Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) is a flagship initiative by the All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE), Ministry of Education. It supports meritorious students from Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh in pursuing undergraduate studies outside their home regions. As of August 22, 2026, this scheme remains a primary pathway for academic mobility.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>Applicants must meet the following criteria to qualify for the scholarship. Failure to meet these requirements will result in disqualification during verification.</p><ul><li><strong>Domicile:</strong> Must be a resident of the Union Territories of Jammu & Kashmir or Ladakh.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Passed 10+2 from JKBOSE or CBSE-affiliated schools in J&K or Ladakh.</li><li><strong>Academic Year:</strong> Passed 10+2 in the 2024-25 or 2025-26 academic sessions.</li><li><strong>Income Limit:</strong> Annual family income must not exceed Rs 8.00 Lakh.</li><li><strong>Entrance Exams:</strong> Must qualify for JEE (Main) or NEET for Engineering and Medical courses, respectively.</li></ul><h2>Financial Benefits and Disbursement</h2><p>The scheme covers academic fees and provides maintenance charges for living expenses. Academic fees are paid directly to the institution, while maintenance charges are sent via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT).</p><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Academic Fee (Per Annum)</th><th>Maintenance Charges (Per Annum)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General Degree</td><td>Up to Rs 30,000</td><td>Rs 1,00,000</td></tr><tr><td>Engineering/Professional</td><td>Up to Rs 1,25,000</td><td>Rs 1,00,000</td></tr><tr><td>Medical/BDS/Nursing</td><td>Up to Rs 3,00,000</td><td>Rs 1,00,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Note: Maintenance charges are disbursed in two equ', '2169', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:14:13');
INSERT INTO `ai_logs` (`id`, `article_id`, `trend_id`, `pipeline_stage`, `prompt_summary`, `response_summary`, `tokens_used`, `success`, `error_message`, `created_at`) VALUES ('1456', NULL, NULL, 'internal_linking', 'Please contextualize internal links in the following article content:\n\nARTICLE CONTENT (HTML):\n<h2>Overview of the Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) 2026</h2><p>The Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) is a flagship initiative by the All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE), Ministry of Education. It supports meritorious students from Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh in pursuing undergraduate studies outside their home regions. As of August 22, 2026, this scheme r', '{\n  \"linked_content\": \"<h2>Overview of the Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) 2026</h2><p>The Prime Minister Special Scholarship Scheme (PMSSS) is a flagship initiative by the All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE), Ministry of Education. It supports meritorious students from Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh in pursuing undergraduate studies outside their home regions. As of August 22, 2026, this scheme remains a primary pathway for academic mobility. For students exploring other financial aid options, the <a href=\'/automation/article/nsp-scholarship-2026-27-registration-guide/\'>NSP Scholarship 2026-27</a> provides additional support opportunities.</p><h2>Eligibility Criteria</h2><p>Applicants must meet the following criteria to qualify for the scholarship. Failure to meet these requirements will result in disqualification during verification.</p><ul><li><strong>Domicile:</strong> Must be a resident of the Union Territories of Jammu & Kashmir or Ladakh.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Passed 10+2 from JKBOSE or CBSE-affiliated schools in J&K or Ladakh.</li><li><strong>Academic Year:</strong> Passed 10+2 in the 2024-25 or 2025-26 academic sessions.</li><li><strong>Income Limit:</strong> Annual family income must not exceed Rs 8.00 Lakh.</li><li><strong>Entrance Exams:</strong> Must qualify for JEE (Main) or NEET for Engineering and Medical courses, respectively. Students preparing for these exams can refer to the <a href=\'/automation/article/jee-main-2027-syllabus-weightage/\'>JEE Main 2027 syllabus</a> or the <a href=\'/automation/article/neet-ug-2026-biology-weightage-guide/\'>NEET UG 2026 biology guide</a> for better preparation.</li></ul><h2>Financial Benefits and Disbursement</h2><p>The scheme covers academic fees and provides maintenance charges for living expenses. Academic fees are paid directly to the institution, while maintenance charges are sent via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT).</p><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Academic Fee ', '2655', '1', NULL, '2026-08-22 07:14:19');
